{"decisions":[{"id":"c4","verdict":"reject","level":"E4","same_as":"","reason":"Turn 9 'No one in the family expected to get a dime from him. It was quite a surprise.' is A narrating the story and providing context about the inheritance. There is no question-response structure, no presupposition trigger (such as 'as you asked' or 'you seem surprised'), and no correction cue indicating B specifically asked about or expressed surprise regarding the inheritance. A is simply continuing their own narrative elaboration.","counterexample":"If B had said 'Did anyone expect that?' or 'I'm surprised he got anything,' then A's response would reflect B's surprise. But no such cue exists in A's turn."},{"id":"c5","verdict":"reject","level":"E4","same_as":"","reason":"Turn 11 'He still has a complaint though.' is A introducing a new narrative point about Michael. 'Still' here means 'in addition to the positive inheritance news' and 'though' is a contrastive discourse marker against the previous good fortune. This is A continuing their own storytelling about Michael's situation, not responding to B expressing a complaint or concern. No presupposition trigger indicates B raised this point.","counterexample":"If B had said 'Does he have any issues with the house?' then A's response would reflect B's concern. But the phrasing is purely A's narrative continuation with no back-reference to B's input."}]}
```

