{"decisions":[{"id":"c6","verdict":"reject","level":"E4","same_as":"","reason":"'Don't stay up late' is an imperative/warning directed at B for the current situation. It does not presuppose a habitual tendency to stay up late. The claim's 'may tend' framing introduces speculation beyond what the directive establishes — a single command does not entail repeated behavior. A parent telling a child not to stay up late tonight does not logically presuppose that the child habitually stays up late.","counterexample":"A parent saying 'Don't stay up late' on a school night to a child who normally sleeps on time — the imperative is a one-time instruction, not a presupposition of habitual lateness."}]}
