{"decisions":[{"id":"c10","verdict":"keep","level":"E3","same_as":"","reason":"Turn 7 asks 'What you would like me to do about it?' and Turn 9 responds 'I won't be able to fix it at the moment.' The direct address to 'fixing' in A's reply strongly presupposes that B's unseen response to turn 7 specifically requested fixing. If B had asked for a different action (e.g., calling a plumber, replacing the faucet entirely), A's response about fixing would be a non-sequitur. The reply-act structure establishes that B's desired action was fixing.","counterexample":""},{"id":"c11","verdict":"reject","level":"E4","same_as":"","reason":"A's statement 'I won't be able to fix it at the moment' is A's own declaration of unavailability. It does not presuppose that B demanded immediate fixing. A could be volunteering this constraint without any time pressure from B. B's temporal preference is not established by A's self-stated limitation. The 'at the moment' phrase is A's framing of their own schedule, not evidence of B's urgency.","counterexample":"A might say 'I won't be able to fix it at the moment' even if B simply asked 'can you fix it sometime?'"}]}
