{"decisions":[{"id":"c1","verdict":"keep","level":"E1","same_as":"","reason":"A's phrase 'after work' directly presupposes B has a job or work; solid E1 presupposition from turn 1.","counterexample":""},{"id":"c2","verdict":"duplicate","level":"E2","same_as":"c1","reason":"Same claim as c1 ('B has a job/works') from the same evidence ('after work'); c1 is the more precise representative.","counterexample":""},{"id":"c3","verdict":"keep","level":"E2","evidence":"A says 'or in vacation', presupposing B has vacation time; distinct from the job presupposition.","same_as":"","reason":"A's phrase 'in vacation' presupposes B has vacation time; this is a distinct claim from having a job.","counterexample":"B might not have vacation time if A was speaking generically."},{"id":"c4","verdict":"keep","level":"E2","same_as":"","reason":"A's 'But traveling is an expensive hobby, isn't it?' uses 'But' (responding to B's prior mention) and 'isn't it?' (seeking confirmation), presupposing B mentioned traveling as a hobby/activity.","counterexample":"A could be introducing the topic unprompted, though 'But' and the tag question strongly suggest a prior mention."}]}
