{"decisions":[{"id":"c2","verdict":"reject","level":"E4","same_as":"","reason":"A's question 'Would you like to make a reservation?' is an offer, not evidence of B's interest. Questions do not establish their own answers; B could decline. No response from B is visible that confirms interest.","counterexample":"B could respond 'No, I was just asking about the location.'"}, {"id":"c5","verdict":"reject","level":"E4","same_as":"","reason":"'If you have many small meeting' is an explicitly conditional/hypothetical suggestion. It does not assert that B actually has many small meetings. The 'if' marker signals a hypothetical scenario, not a presupposition about B's real situation.","counterexample":"A is offering a general suggestion applicable to any caller who might have that need."}, {"id":"c8","verdict":"reject","level":"E4","same_as":"","reason":"A proactively offers 'Would you like to make a reservation?' following 'You're in luck!' which responds to B mentioning a location. There is no evidence B specifically asked about making a reservation; A is volunteering the offer.","counterexample":"B may have simply stated a destination or asked about proximity, prompting A to proactively offer a reservation."}]}
