{"decisions":[{"id":"c3","verdict":"reject","level":"E4","same_as":"","reason":"Turn 3 is a direct question ('Have you written down potatoes, carrots, and onions?') asking whether B performed the action. Questions do not establish their answers. The 'may have' hedge in the claim makes it speculative rather than a grounded attribute of B. No definite information about B's list contents is conveyed.","counterexample":"If B answered 'No, I forgot,' the claim would be false, demonstrating the question does not establish the answer."},{"id":"c6","verdict":"reject","level":"E4","same_as":"","reason":"Turn 11 'Shall I drive?' is A volunteering or proposing to drive. This does not presuppose that B was expected to drive or has been driving. The offer to drive suggests the driving arrangement is undetermined or that A is taking initiative, not that B holds a driving role. No attribute of B is established.","counterexample":"If B answered 'No, I'll drive,' the claim that B was expected to drive or has been driving would be unsupported by A's turn."}]}
