{"decisions":[{"id":"c1","verdict":"reject","level":"E4","same_as":"","reason":"Turn 3 uses third-person 'He's a year older than Keith,' which refers to a third party (the retired person discussed in turn 5), not B. If A were describing B, the expected form would be 'You're a year older than Keith.'","counterexample":"A is talking about B's brother or friend who retired, not about B."},{"id":"c2","verdict":"reject","level":"E4","same_as":"","reason":"Turn 3's 'but he looks younger' uses third-person pronoun 'he,' referring to the same third party as 'He's a year older than Keith.' This does not describe B's appearance.","counterexample":"The retired third person looks younger than Keith; nothing is said about B's appearance."},{"id":"c3","verdict":"reject","level":"E4","same_as":"","reason":"Turn 7's 'He wants to travel to several different countries around the world' uses third-person 'he,' continuing the description of the retired third party from turn 5. B's own desires are not stated; turn 9 asks B a question about how B wants to spend old age, which does not establish an answer.","counterexample":"The retired person wants to travel; B has not yet answered turn 9's question about their own plans."}]}
